License, Version 2.0. All adapted parts were modified by PlateerLab. Each
adapted file carries a "Portions adapted from google-research/rrsi" header.

Adapted parts:

1. Code structure (module layout, control flow, data formats):
   - xgen_rsi/evolve/round.py, frontier.py, driver.py  <- rrsi/loop.py, rrsi/driver.py
     (round structure, frontier.json layout, sequential driver)
   - xgen_rsi/evolve/history.py                        <- rrsi/history.py
   - xgen_rsi/evolve/gitops.py                         <- rrsi/gitops.py
   - xgen_rsi/evolve/config.py                         <- rrsi/config.py
   - xgen_rsi/evolve/analyst.py, digester.py,
     propose.py, critic.py                             <- rrsi/analyst.py, digester.py,
                                                          propose.py, critic.py
   - xgen_rsi/rsi_math/rrsi.py, types.py               <- rrsi/schedule.py, evaluate.py,
                                                          selection.py, history.py,
                                                          components.py
     (formula semantics reproduced and verified by differential tests
     against the reference)
   - xgen_rsi/rsi_math/calibrate.py                    <- rrsi/calibrate.py
   - small JSON-extraction helpers in xgen_rsi/roles/llm.py and
     xgen_rsi/evolve/verifiers.py                      <- rrsi/llm.py

2. Role prompt texts: the analyst and trace-digester prompts and digest
   schemas, the proposer prompt and its JSON action protocol, and the leakage
   critic's review rules and generic credential patterns
   (xgen_rsi/evolve/analyst.py, digester.py, propose.py, critic.py), adapted
   from the corresponding reference modules and extended with XGEN-specific
   rules.

3. Proposer constitution and pattern library: the section structure, hard
   rules and rule texts of xgen_rsi/evolve/constitution/SKILL.md (from
   domains/*/SKILL.md, mainly coding and eng) and the pattern-library format
   of xgen_rsi/evolve/constitution/PATTERNS.md (from domains/*/PATTERNS.md),
   rewritten for XGEN business-agent harnesses.

The Dream-RSI method (arXiv:2609.14858) and the RRSI method (arXiv:2609.24972)
are implemented from the papers' descriptions. The papers themselves are not
redistributed in this repository; see the arXiv pages. Apart from the parts
listed above, prompts in this repository are written for this project; where
a prompt follows a paper's published rules, the rules are restated in our own
words.
